  body: "# Relevant change of circumstances for supersession\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor supersession,
    the captured guidance asks whether a change after the decision took effect is relevant to the benefit award,
    with a separate route for expected changes and qualifications for disallowed claims.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nNot every change produces a changed award. The general fresh-claim rule after disallowance has the stated
    DMG 04103 exception; a change of opinion and a change of law need separate treatment. No reporting deadline
    is inferred.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 04100, PDF page 16](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=16)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04102, PDF page 17](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=17)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04103, PDF page 17](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=17)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04104, PDF page 18](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=18)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n- `dmg-vol1-ch3`
    PDF SHA-256: `4aebcf1988fb7d96698dce77bf88d68272a5975171decc42f58c32cfa1d42eeb`; extracted pages SHA-256: `444fa1a240db31b94cb75c13a2f2ece7c691f15aeca0bec2dd298e2f4e08f66a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passage associates an actual or expected relevant change with possible supersession,
      without saying supersession is automatic.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0016
      quote: "04100 Where\n\n\n1. there has been a relevant change of circumstances since the decision\n\n\n   \
        \   1.1 had effect or\n\n\n      1.2 was made in the case of an advance award1 or\n\n\n2. it is expected
        that a change will occur\n\n\nthe DM may supersede the decision which is currently in force2. The application
        period for revision is\nirrelevant in these cases. See also DMG 04115 - 04116.\n\n\n                   \
        \                     1 SS (C&P) Regs, reg 13, 13A & 13C; 2 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 6(2)(a)"
      locator: DMG 04100
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The revision chapter distinguishes reporting a change from revising a decision and routes it to
      claim or supersession rules.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0003
      quote: "03004 (see DMG memo 13-22) A decision cannot be revised where claimants report a change of\ncircumstances
        during the application period. The claim or supersession rules apply instead (see DMG"
      locator: DMG 03004
